From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:43:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Added KEV and EPSS data to reports and finding pages

Report data now gives each finding its stored KEV and EPSS facts:
- kev, kev_cves, kev_due_date and kev_ransomware;
- epss_max, epss_max_percentile, epss_max_cve and epss_over_threshold;
- a per-CVE vuln_intel list.
The report-level vuln_intel holds the catalog version and the dates the data
was current. Three totals count KEV, ransomware and high-EPSS findings. The
template linter has samples for every key, and a test keeps them in step with
the real data.

The Excel report adds KEV, KEV Due Date, Known Ransomware Use, Highest EPSS
and EPSS Percentile columns. Library finding pages show KEV and EPSS badges
per CVE ID. The findings library and report findings tables show one KEV badge
and the highest EPSS score per finding, from one lookup per page.

A new EPSS threshold setting highlights high scores and drives the totals.
KEV release dates now parse on Pythons older than 3.11.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JeRCvM2shAtegxe489Vfvx
